cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "OPAAS — On-Prem AI Audit Suite"
message: "If you use OPAAS in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "onpremIALabs"
    website: "https://onpremialabs.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/luxinopanyvino/opaas-bench"
url: "https://onpremialabs.com"
abstract: >-
  OPAAS audits an LLM or SLM deployment rather than a model: the composite of
  model, quantization, inference engine, hardware and configuration. It reports
  per category with confidence intervals, never as an aggregate score, declares
  what it could not measure instead of reporting a zero, and uses no LLM judge
  anywhere in scoring, so a third party can recompute a figure rather than trust
  it. Reports are canonical JCS bytes whose SHA-256 is the certified hash, and
  can be signed as W3C Verifiable Credentials and verified offline.
keywords:
  - llm
  - slm
  - evaluation
  - audit
  - quantization
  - inference
  - on-premise
  - edge-ai
  - reproducibility
  - verifiable-credentials
license: MIT
version: 0.2.1
date-released: 2026-10-15
